agentd — third-party material vendored into this repository
===========================================================

agentd's own source is AGPL-3.0-only (see LICENSE), with one deliberate
exception: `crates/instruction` (published as `agentd-instruction`) is
`MIT OR Apache-2.0` from 0.2.0, so that other implementations of the
Instruction Specification can link the reference implementation rather than
reimplement it. See `crates/instruction/NOTICE`. Some files in this tree
come from elsewhere and carry their own terms. They are listed here because a
licence statement that names only the project's own licence is silent about
precisely the files someone might copy out of it.

The Instruction Specification (https://github.com/instruction-md/specification),
owned by instruction.md. agentd is its reference implementation, so two
artifacts are vendored rather than referenced — a contract that only holds
where someone happens to have a checkout does not hold.

1. `crates/instruction/src/instruction.schema.json`
   The specification's machine-readable registry (kinds, forms, grants,
   semantic rules). Licence: **CC BY 4.0** — the specification repository's
   root LICENSE. Attribution: "The Instruction Specification", instruction.md,
   https://github.com/instruction-md/specification. Vendored so the parser
   reads its kind registry from the specification itself and cannot drift from
   it; `the_vendored_schema_matches_upstream_when_present` checks the copy
   against the published original.

2. `crates/instruction/tests/conformance/**`
   The specification's conformance fixtures, the whole directory as upstream
   publishes it: `corpus/` (delivered text, block trees, resolution
   manifests), `refusals/`, `advisories/`, and the `README.md` and `LICENSE`
   that accompany them — the shared fixtures the Rust and TypeScript
   implementations are both held to. Licence: **Apache-2.0**, every file of it,
   `advisories/` included — see `crates/instruction/tests/conformance/LICENSE`,
   copied alongside the fixtures with the README as that licence requires.
   Vendored so the suite runs everywhere rather than only where a sibling
   checkout exists; `the_vendored_corpus_matches_upstream_when_present` checks
   every file against the published fixtures in both directions.

The Personal Agent Protocol (https://personalagentprotocol.org,
https://github.com/personal-agent-protocol/personal-agent-protocol). agentd's
Personal Agent support is built against one revision of the draft, so that
revision is vendored rather than referenced — the draft moves without a
version signal.

3. `crates/agentd/tests/companies/vendor/**`
   The draft at commit 95fcbf22c5991a0090061aed3dbeb68c0ea575e0, verbatim, as
   its `PIN` file maps it: the 19 JSON Schemas of the Company kit, and the
   Markdown renderings of the specification, the Operations extension and the
   guides. Licence: **Apache-2.0** — see
   `crates/agentd/tests/companies/vendor/LICENSE`, copied alongside, and
   `crates/agentd/NOTICE`. The licence does not cover the names "Personal
   Agent Protocol" and "Poppy", the logo or the site's design; the vendored
   files keep the names as written, and agentd's own surface does not use
   them. `the_vendored_draft_matches_upstream_when_present` checks every file
   against the pinned commit.

Both licences are compatible with distributing this repository under the AGPL:
CC BY 4.0 and Apache-2.0 permit redistribution with attribution, which this
notice and the copied LICENSE files provide. No vendored artifact is compiled
into a release binary as code — the instruction schema is read as data, the
corpus and the draft's pages are test input, and the draft's schemas are read
as data by the fake Company, test scaffolding that only debug builds and
`internal-mocks` builds with `oauth` (and the default `tls`) carry.
